  3194	        # arriving during the `await asyncio.gather` below would spawn
  3195	        # a fresh _process_message_background task (added to
  3196	        # self._background_tasks at line ~1668 via handle_message),
  3197	        # and the _background_tasks.clear() at the end of this method
  3198	        # would drop the reference — the task runs untracked against a
  3199	        # disconnecting adapter, logs send-failures, and may linger
  3200	        # until it completes on its own.  Retrying the drain until the
  3201	        # task set stabilizes closes the window.
